@startuml gameplay-sequence
title Play a Domino Match — invalid retry and confirmed placement
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
autonumber
actor "Active player" as Player
boundary "Player client" as Client
control "Authoritative game service" as Game
collections "All participant clients" as All
note over Player, All
  Precondition: full, configured match has been dealt and opened.
  2/3: individual draw; 4: fixed opposing-seat teams, block.
  This example shows one placement turn, not a fixed round of four turns.
end note
Player -> Client: Choose an illegal tile/end
Client -> Game: Request placement(tile, end)
Game -> Game: Validate turn, ownership and matching end
Game --> Client: Reject illegal placement (confirmed)
note right of Game
  State and active participant unchanged.
  An out-of-turn request is rejected identically.
end note
Client --> Player: Show reason; allow retry
Player -> Client: Choose a legal tile/end
Client -> Game: Request placement(tile, end)
Game -> Game: Revalidate against current state
alt Still legal and player's turn
  Game -> Game: Apply placement; remove tile; reset passes
  alt Hand now empty
    Game -> Game: Finish immediately: player (2/3) or team (4) wins
    Game --> Client: Confirm placement and final result
    Game -> All: Broadcast final state and result
    Client --> Player: Display confirmed result
    note right of Game: No next turn after a terminal placement.
  else Tiles remain
    Game -> Game: Advance active participant in seat order (wrap)
    Game --> Client: Confirm placement and next participant
    Game -> All: Broadcast updated state and next participant
    Client --> Player: Display confirmed state
  end
else No longer valid / out of turn
  Game --> Client: Reject; no state or turn change
  Client --> Player: Show rejection and current confirmed state
end
note over Client, All
  Broadcast includes the acting client; it is not a separate extra participant.
  Share board, turn, counts and result; each hand is private to its owner.
  If confirmation is not received, the client must not claim success.
  Missing delivery does not imply server rejection; recovery is unresolved.
  Draw/pass and blocked-game resolution are in the activity diagram.
end note
@enduml
